Modes: Orchestrator

Purpose:
  Defines orchestrator modes and decision thresholds.

Modes:
  AUTO: AI decides low-risk items
  SUPERVISED: AI recommends, human approves major decisions
  STRICT: Human approval required for architecture, security, DB migration, release
  AUDIT: Analysis only, no modifications
  READ_ONLY: Project analysis, no code changes

DecisionThreshold:
  LOW_RISK: AI decides
  MEDIUM_RISK: AI recommends
  HIGH_RISK: Human approval
  CRITICAL: Human mandatory

HumanDecisionBoundary:
  AI decides: code implementation, test creation, documentation, non-security configuration
  Human approves: architecture changes, database migration, security policy, production destructive operations

Degradation:
  FULL: all features operational
  REDUCED: skip optional stages, core skills only
  MINIMAL: basic chain only, human approval for all gates
  READ_ONLY: analysis only, no modifications
  Triggers: resource pressure, component failure, repeated failures

Rules:
  [MD1] Default mode is AUTO for standard projects.
  [MD2] STRICT mode requires human approval for critical decisions.
  [MD3] READ_ONLY mode never modifies source code.
  [MD4] Complexity budget MUST be respected.
  [MD5] Degradation is automatic based on health checks.
  [MD6] Recovery is automatic when conditions improve.
  [MD7] Human is notified of mode changes.

State: +